  {
   "id": "edit-remarks",
   "type": "text",
   "value": "Mid-infrared eruption found in archival WISE/NEOWISE data by Oddsky (oddsky.ai): difference imaging of the unWISE time-resolved coadds (NEO11 version, courtesy A. Meisner; Meisner, Lang & Schlegel 2018) against a 2014.8-2023.2 reference. Nothing at this position in 18 W1/W2 epochs from 2014-10 to 2023-03-27. First detected 2023-10-23 at W1 = 18.18 +- 0.07 and W2 = 18.05 +- 0.12 AB; on 2024-03-28, the last NEOWISE epoch here, W1 = 16.71 +- 0.02 and W2 = 16.36 +- 0.02 AB, still rising. Magnitudes are of the difference flux; the flux-scale systematic is about 0.1 mag. An earlier infrared event at the same position: public Spitzer/IRAC 3.6 um images show +0.22 mJy on 2009-11-25, declining to +0.13 mJy by 2010-04/06, after a flat 2003-2005, and WISE 2010 was still above the 2014-2023 level. The source lies in the HII region [HAE2008] 7; Gaia DR3 1070474934439610752 (G = 20.25, BP-RP = 0.37) is 0.28\" away. No ZTF alert object within 35\". ATLAS forced photometry shows no brightening at the WISE epochs (3-sigma limits c > 21.3, o > 21.2 AB). 351\" NW of the centre of M81. No spectrum."
  },
